I stopped without making any changes: issue #261 can't move forward from this run. I've labelled it `needs-decision` and posted the questions on it ([comment](https://github.com/tacplus-dev/tacplus/issues/261#issuecomment-6728636957)). Nothing was committed or landed.

**Why I stopped:**
- **The spike can't be run from here.** The issue says to run it first, on the Mac runner. That runner belongs to the GitLab project tacplus-dev/build, which only runs protected-ref jobs started from the web. This run has no GitLab token (the API returns 401) and can't see that project (404), the same limit looper#36 hit.
- **Most of the work is in other repositories.** The build and verify jobs and the move of `macos-smoke` go in tacplus-dev/looper's `ci/build.gitlab-ci.yml`. The wrapper that refuses host mounts goes in the GitLab project's `mac-runner/`. The job VM's disk size is set in the runner's host config. Only the install script, the version pins and the docs belong in this repository.

**Decisions I asked for, with my recommendations:**
- **A. Registry:** use GCP Artifact Registry through the existing workload identity setup. The images are on ghcr.io today, but a GitLab job can't get a ghcr.io push token that way without a stored GitHub credential, which the issue rules out.
- **B. Who pushes:** the issue contradicts itself. Its body has the guest push the image, but Jody's later comment has `tart push` run on the host. I recommend the guest; pushing from the host would put a registry credential there.
- **C. Who does what:** the pipeline jobs go in tacplus-dev/looper, and someone with access to the GitLab project runs the spike and adds the wrapper. I asked whether I should open the looper issue.
- **D. Disk size:** it has to be set in the runner's host config, since the wrapper will refuse jobs that try to set it. I asked whether it applies to this one job or to all `macos` jobs.
- **E. Matching Rust versions:** `build.Dockerfile` uses the floating `rust:1`, so `build:X.Y`'s Rust changes on each rebuild. The acceptance criterion that both images have the same Rust needs an exact pin.
- **F. One source of truth:** an `images/versions.env` that both images read, with a test that fails if `build.Dockerfile`'s pins drift from it. I can build that here once A–E are settled.

The checkpoint on `looper/tacplus-261` contains only the looper's own run files (`.looper/`). Once Jody answers and removes the label, the next run picks this up again.
